/HELP1
			INVOICE HELP SCREEN ONE
==============================================================================

The invoice creation and printing configuration demonstrates a "programmed"
DataFlex application.  It does not use a standard "enter" format.  The
intent of this configuration is to allow the operator to enter up to six
line items on one screen and then to print the invoice, update inventory
and the customer record, all on line.

The invoice creation is in two parts, header information and line items.
Both sections operate very much like an enter configuration to enhance
consistency of use.  Once both sections are completed, hit the ESCAPE key
and you will be given the oportunity to print or cancel the invoice.  The
file updates take place AFTER the invoice is printed.

INVOICE NUMBER: First you must enter the invoвZЊРЋА‹ьѓп^ЊЫ№␀ѓм
уҐЋЫявU‹мЌvЊРЊЫЋШД~№␀уҐ]ZѓДЋЫяв␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀s screen.

	DISPLAY DAYS.1& TO DATE.3
//use indexed window addressing to display the day of the week to the user.
	RETURN

KEYPROC KEY.FIELD
	BACKFIELD		//back up one window
	RETURN
KEYPROC KEY.ESCAPE
	ABORT			// go away and dont save record

KEYPROC KEY.HELP		//set up confiuration for help screens
	HELP			//show the help screen
	ENTAGAIN		//back to same window
	RETURN			//return to accept
confiuration for help screens
	HELP			//show the help screen
	ENTAGAIN		//back to same window
	RETUAL 
  SUBTOTAL BODY.4		//subtotal will take the accumulator
				//for any numeric window and print
				//it in another window. 
				//print the total purchases for all
  OUTPUT TOTAL			//customers in the database
REPORTEND
ABORT


another windowцбЉђµ␀Бў“лЭ “Љ’·␀€‡XЂыu<v°PиЌл “‹€G-й!яи*ьўЗ]Г␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ice number to print.

You may FIND the correct customer by either customer number or name.  If you
want to find by name, press return on customer #.  You may then find by
customer name using the standard FLEX KEY's.  You must find a valid customer 
to continue.
/HELP2
		     INVOICE HELP SCREEN TWO
=========================================================================

DISC: DISCOUNT, the discount from the customer file will display here.
You may override this and enter a new discount.

TERMS: Terms in days.	VIA: Ship via?	   SLSMN: Salesman name or initl.

CUSTOMER ORDER: The customers order or P.O. reference.

The rest of the entry portion refers to the line item section.	Within
line items you may use the up and down arrows to edit the invoice and
the delete key will delete one line item.

PART ID: You may find the part in question by part ID or description. All
the standard flex keys apply.  This is "YOUR PART ID" on the inventory
screen.

The default price will display from the/INV	
DATA ACCESS CORPORATION 					      INVOICE
=============================================================================

INVOICE NUMBER: _____.				CUSTOMER# ___.	

	BILL TO: ______________________________
		 ______________________________
		 ______________  __  __________

DISC  TERMS    DATE	 VIA		 SLSMN	   CUSTOMER ORDER
  _.	__.  __/__/__	 ____________	 ____	   ______________
..............................................................................
   PART ID	   DESCRIPTION				  PRICE  QTY	AMOUNT
   --------------- ----------------------------------- -------- ---- ---------
1. _______________ ___________________________________ _____.__ ___. ______.__
2. _______________ ___________________________________ _____.__ ___. ______.__
3. _______________ ___________________________________ _____.__ ___. ______.__
4. _______________ ___________________________________ _____.__ ___. ______.__
5. _______________ ___________________________________ _____.__ ___. ______.__
6. __________ inventory file, you may use or
override the price.

When done hit ESCAPE to print the invoice.
/READY
DATA ACCESS CORPORATION 				    INVOICE PRINTING
============================================================================



  READY TO PRINT INVOICE #________.


  Check the status of your printer for invoice printing and, 

  PRESS:   RETURN TO CONTINUE AND PRINT INVOICE.
	   ESCAPE TO CANCEL THIS INVOICE.
	   BACK FIELD TO EDIT INVOICE			_

/*
	NAME INV INVNUM
	AUTOPAGE INV 14
	NAME PART DSCR PRICE QTY AMOUNT NXTPART
	AUTOPAGE INV 44
	NAME PR1 VEND PR2 VENDPART PR3 STOCK TOTAL
	INTEGER LINEITEM MAXLINE COUNTER
	NUMBER DISCOUNT
		STRING TEMP
	OUTFILE 		// PICK UP OUTPUT DEVICE FROM CMDLINE
	MOVE 33 TO PAGEFEED	// HALF PAGE INVOICE


	OPEN ITEMS		//INVENTORY TRANSACTIONS
	OPEN INVT		//INVENTORY
	OPEN CUSTOMER		//CUSTOMERS
	OPEN SYSFILE		//SYSTEM DATE FILE

	AUTOPAGE INV			// use page INV automaticlly
INVSTART:
	  INDICATE INHEADER TRUE
// inheader indicates that wce cursor on correct line item.
// All line item windows must then have a "&" after them to 
// indicate indexed addressing.

// We can use an entergroup to process each line item also.
// Each entergroup operates like a small internal enter configuration.
	    CLEAR INVT
	    ENTERGROUP
		ENTRY INVT.PART_ID	   PART&    {AUTOFIND,NOPUT}
		ENTRY INVT.DESCRIPTION	   DSCR&    {NOPUT,FINDREQ,SKIPFOUND}
		ENTRY INVT.LIST_PRICE	   PRICE&   {DISPLAYONLY}
		ENTRY INVT.VENDOR	   VEND     {DISPLAYONLY}
		ENTRY INVT.VENDOR_PART_ID  VENDPART {DISPLAYONLY}
		ENTRY INVT.QUANTITY	   STOCK    {DISPLAYONLY}

TR3:		ACCEPT QTY&		//Quantity sold
		IF QTY& GT INVT.QUANTITY BEGIN
			ERROR 101
			GOTO TR3
			END
		ENDGROUP

		DISPLAY (PRICE&*QTY&*DISCOUNT) TO AMOUNT& // extend price
		DISPLAY (INV.18+INV.23+INV.28+INV.33+INV.38+INV.43) TO TOTAL
// END OF LINE ITEM
		INCREMENT LINEITEM
// start on next line item
		IF LINEITEM GT MAXLINE MOVE LINEITEM TO MAXLINE
// increment maxline if we are on the last le are in the invoice header portion.
// Some of the flex keys should function differently in the header
// or line item sections.
	  MOVE 0 TO MAXLINE		// use printers form feed.
	  CLEARFORM INV.2 THRU READY.1	// clear invoice page.
	  MOVE 'MEMORY = ' TO PR2	// show memory
	  MOVE MEMAVAIL TO VENDPART	// at first.
	  ACCEPT			// accept from first window
					// note autopage above.
	  CLEAR INVT			// clear these files
	  CLEAR ITEMS
	  CLEAR CUSTOMER

	  AUTOPAGE INV 2		// restart autopage on window 2

	  ENTERGROUP			
// use entergroup for finding  and display of the customer record.
// since entergroup provides all of the standard flex key operations
// about three times as much code would be required without it.
	      ENTRY CUSTOMER.RECNUM	{AUTOFIND,NOPUT}
	      ENTRY CUSTOMER.CUSTOMER	{NOPUT, FINDREQ, SKIPFOUND }
	      ENTRY CUSTOMER.ADDRESS	{DISPLAYONLY}
	      ENTRY CUSTOMER.CITY	{DISPLAYONLY}
	      ENTRY CUSTOMER.STATE	{DISPLAYONLY}
	      ENTRY CUSTOMER.ZIP	{DISPLAYONLY}ine item (as usual)
		IF LINEITEM LT 6 GOTO TR1
// if all 6 locations full, print invoice.

 //////////// BOTTEM OF INPUT LOOP /////////////////////

// ask operator to verify invoice.
PRINTIT:	MOVE INV.1 TO READY.1
		INDICATE VERINV TRUE
		REPEAT
		    ACCEPT READY.2
[NOT KEY.RETURN]    LOOP

// ok to print invoice if here.
		INDICATE VERINV FALSE
		INDICATE ENDINV TRUE

// The following loop goes thru all of the line items to update
// It's better to do it here because the inoice is confirmed.
		MOVE 0 TO WINDOWINDEX	// init to line item one.

		FOR COUNTER FROM 1 TO 6 // do six line items
		IF PART& GT '' BEGIN	// if part is '', end of invoice
		// CREATE TRANSACTION
			CLEAR ITEMS	// clear the files for find
			CLEAR INVT
			MOVE PART& TO INVT.PART_ID	// find by part id
			FIND GE INVT.PART_ID
			IF QTY& GT INVT.QUANTITY BEGIN
			    MOVE (INVT.QUANTITY>0) TO QTY&
		DISPLAY (PRICE&*QTY&*DISCOUNT) TO AMOUNT& // extend price
		DISPLAY (INV.18+INV.23+INV.28+INV.33+INV.38+INV.43
	      ENDGROUP

// display and accept header information
	  DISPLAY CUSTOMER.DISCOUNT TO INV.8	//DEFAULT DISCOUNT
	  ACCEPT
	  CALC (100-INV.8/100) TO DISCOUNT
	  DISPLAY 30 TO INV.9			//DEFAULT TERMS
	  ACCEPT			 
	  DISPLAY SYSFILE.DATE TO INV.10
	  ACCEPT
	  ACCEPT				// VIA
	  ACCEPT				// SLSMN
	  ACCEPT				// CUST ORD

// <<<<<<<<<<<<< LINE ITEM ENTRY SECTION >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
LITEM:
	  MOVE 0 TO LINEITEM
// Lineitem variable keeps track of which line item we are processing.
// This information is used to calculate the indexed addressing required
// where there are multiple items from the same file on the screen at
// one time.

	  GOSUB PROMPTS 		// print prompts for vendor info.

DOLINE: 
// This is the main line item entry loop.

                INDICATE VERINV FALSE
		INDICATE INHEADER FALSE
		INDICATE ENDINV FALSE
// inheader and endinv are used by key procedures.

	// FIND BY PART ID //
TR1:		CALC (LINEITEM*5) TO WINDOWINDEX
// Compute window index to pla) TO TOTAL
			    PAD DSCR& TO TEMP 20
			    APPEND TEMP " <<LOW STOCK>>"
			    MOVE TEMP TO DSCR&
			    ERROR 101 // OUT OF STOCK
			    END

			MOVE INVNUM TO ITEMS.INVOICE	// fill in trans rec.
			MOVE QTY& TO ITEMS.QUANTITY
			MOVE PRICE& TO ITEMS.PRICE
			MOVE AMOUNT& TO ITEMS.AMOUNT
			MOVE (QTY&*INVT.AVG_COST) TO ITEMS.COST
			MOVE INVT.VENDOR TO ITEMS.VENDOR

			REREAD INVT	// MULTIUSER REREAD
       //UPDATE INVENTORY RECORD
       CALC (INVT.QUANTITY-QTY&) TO INVT.QUANTITY
       CALC (INVT.SALES_MONTH+AMOUNT&) TO INVT.SALES_MONTH
       CALC (INVT.SALES_YEAR+AMOUNT&) TO INVT.SALES_YEAR
       CALC (INVT.PROFIT_YEAR+AMOUNT&-ITEMS.COST) TO INVT.PROFIT_YEAR
			SAVE INVT	// save old invt record for update.
			SAVE ITEMS	// save new items transaction
			UNLOCK
			END
		      CALC (WINDOWINDEX+5) TO WINDOWINDEX
// compute next line item line in the invoice. 
		      LOOP    // LINE ITEMS

// update customer record already found in header.
		REREAD CUSTOMER 	// MULTIUSER REORM PART& THRU INV.43	// and clear it
		DISPLAY (INV.18+INV.23+INV.28+INV.33+INV.38+INV.43) TO TOTAL
// update total
		RETURN DOLINE

PROMPTS:	DISPLAY 'VENDOR:' TO PR1
		DISPLAY 'VEND PART:' TO PR2
		DISPLAY 'STOCK QTY' TO PR3
		RETURN

KEYERROR:		// if bad flex key is pressed
	  ENTAGAIN
	  ERROR 100
	  RETURN

  IF STROKE EQ "" GOTO WAITKEY	//loop until keypressed

	    END 	//end finderr block

	    RETURN
