DATA ACCESS CORPORATION 			INVENTORY MASTER FILE
=====================================================================

       VENDOR NUMBER:<__.>     NAME:<______________________________>

      VENDOR PART ID:<_______________>

	YOUR PART ID:<_______________>

	 DESCRIPTION:<___________________________________>

      STOCK QUANTITY:	_____.		MINIMUM QUANTITY: _.  

    REORDER QUANTITY:	_____.		  QTY ON ORDER: _____ 

	SALES/MONTH: $________.__	 SALES/YEAR: $________.__

	PROFIT/YEAR: $	______.__

	 LIST PRICE: $	______.__     WHOLESALE PRICE: $______.__  

       AVERAGE COST: $	______.__	STOCK VALUE: $________.__
/HELP1	    HELP
			INVENTORY ENTRY HELP SCREEN
============================================================================

The inventory entry screen is intended for the creation and maintenance of
the inventory file in the DataFlex demonstration application.  This is a
standard "ENTER" screen and as such uses the standard "flex keys".  Oper- 
ations that canin verify cancel
	     RETURN PRINTIT	// else print

KEYPROC KEY.UP
[INHEADER]	GOTO KEYERROR
[ENDINV]	GOTO KEYERROR
// back up one line item
		IF LINEITEM EQ 0 GOTO KEYERROR
		CALC (LINEITEM-1) TO LINEITEM
		RETURN DOLINE

KEYPROC KEY.DOWN
[INHEADER]	GOTO KEYERROR
[ENDINV]	GOTO KEYERROR
// down one line item
		IF PART& EQ '' GOTO KEYERROR
		IF LINEITEM GE 5 RETURN
		CALC (LINEITEM+1) TO LINEITEM
		RETURN DOLINE

KEYPROC KEY.DELETE
[INHEADER]	GOTO KEYERROR	// invalid
[ENDINV]	GOTO KEYERROR	// invalid
// this will delete one line item and move the rest up one line.
		IF PART& EQ '' GOTO KEYERROR
		BLANKFORM VEND
		INTEGER TOWINDOW FROMWINDOW STOPAT
// calculate start and end windows to move
		MOVE (MAXLINE*5-1) TO STOPAT
// loop to move line items

                FOR WINDOWINDEX FROM WINDOWINDEX TO STOPAT
                        MOVESTR NXTPART& TO PART&
			LOOP

		MOVE ( MAXLINE-1) TO MAXLINE	// update maxline
		MOVE (MAXLINE*5) TO WINDOWINDEX // look at last line
		CLEARF be proformed are; Inventory record Creation, Deletion, 
Editing and Inspection.

The inventory file is indexed and can therefore be found three ways.

	1) By vendor number, THEN vendor ID.
	2) By "your part id"
	3) By description.

Move the cursor over the field you wish to find by and press the "FIND" key.

Two fields from the vendor file are also displayed on this screen, Vendor ID 
and Vendor Name.  The correct vendor can be found by either key field.

For more help on individual fields press the help key again, otherwise
press any other key to return to the inventory screen.
/HELP2 HELP
		    INVENTORY HELP SCREEN TWO
========================================================================

VENDOR NUMBER: If you know the vendor's number, enter the number here
otherwise press return.

VENDOR NAME: If you entered a valid number the cursor will skip this field,
otherwise you may use the flex keys to find a valid vendor by name.  A vendor
MUST be found to continue.

YOUR PART ID: Ie used in a case like this.
	 ENTRY VENDOR.VENDOR	     {SKIPFOUND,findreq}
// Translation, Do data entry on the vendor name of the vendor file
// Skip this entry if a record has alredy been found and REQUIRE
// that a vendor be found to continue.
	 ENTRY INVT.VENDOR_PART_ID   {SKIPFOUND,RETAIN}
// Translation, Do data entry on the vendor part id of the inventory
// file.  Skip this is a record has been found (preventing changes)
// and retain the entry after a clear window command.
	 ENTRY INVT.PART_ID	     {RETAINALL,REQUIRED}
	 ENTRY INVT.DESCRIPTION      {CAPSLOCK}
	 ENTRY INVT.QUANTITY
	 ENTRY INVT.MINIMUM
	 ENTRY INVT.REORDER	     
	 ENTRY INVT.ON_ORDER	     
 // These fields do not use autopage, they name each window.
 // Either form is acceptable.
	 ENTRY INVT.SALES_MONTH       FORM.10	{DISPLAYONLY}
	 ENTRY INVT.SALES_YEAR	      FORM.11	{DISPLAYONLY}
	 ENTRY INVT.PROFIT_YEAR       FORM.12
	 ENTRY INVT.LIST_PRICE	      FORM.13
	 ENTRY INVT.WHOLESALE_PRICE   FORM.14
	 ENTRY INVT.AVGs a required field, this is your "in house" part number.

DESCRIPTION: A description of the part that will be shown on the invoice.

STOCK QUANTITY: Is the number of units in stock.

MINIMUM: Is the reorder point. Quantities in stock less than this should be
	reordered.

REORDER: Is the number of units that should be reordered at one time.

QTY ON ORDER: Is the number that has been previously ordered.

Press HELP for more help otherwise press any key to continue.
/HELP3 HELP 
			INVENTORY HELP SCREEN THREE
============================================================================

SALES/MONTH, SALES/YEAR, PROFIT/YEAR: will be maintained automatically by
the INVOICE screen.  You may want to initalize them with the beginning values.

LIST PRICE: The price you sell the product for (less discounts).

WHOLESALE PRICE: Reference wholesale price.

AVERAGE COST: Average cost of the units in stock.

STOCK VALUE: Is computed as quantity in stock times average cost.

The USER DEFINED key w_COST	      FORM.15
	 ENTRY (INVT.QUANTITY*INVT.LIST_PRICE) FORM.16
// The above is the display of a calculated field.
	 RETURN 	// return is required at the end of the entry section.
	ENTEREND	// as is ENTEREND.
	ABORT		// After the ESCAPE key is hit, abort.

KEYPROC KEY.USER	// Define action of user defined key
	OUTPUT FORM	// Output form to list 
	ENTAGAIN	// Return to same window
	RETURN
.USER	// Define action of user defined key
	OUTPUT FORM	// Output form to list 
	ENTAGAIN	// Return to RN			//return to accept
confiuration for help screens
	HELP			//show the help screen
	ENTAGAIN		//back to same window
	RETUAL 
  SUBTOTAL BODY.4		//subtotal will take the accumulator
				//for any numeric window and print
				//it in another window. 
				//print the total purchases for all
  OUTPUT TOTAL			//customers in the database
REPORTEND
ABORT


