/MEM	HELP
No further help available, please refer to notes on screen. MEMORY=_________
/FMAT
------------------------------ READ ASCII FILE ---------------------------

Some ASCII files have each element or field on a seprate line such that   
multiple lines make up one record, This is a LINE delimited file.

Other files have all of the elements or fields on one line with a comma
between each field and text fields have quotes around them.  This is
called a COMMA delimited file.

IS YOUR ASCII FILE LINE OR COMMA DELIMITED? _____


In either case you must know how many fields must be read for each record.

HOW MANY FIELDS PER RECORD READ? __.


/NAMES
